Prelimiary Proposal
Team 16: Jack Ngo(CE), Owen Klobucher(CE), Wil Dems(CE), Quinn Carolan(CE), Eric Tang(CE)

Project Idea: 
Our current idea is Lodestone. A low-cost and long-battery life wearable that logs your path with GNSS, 
shares it with teammates over LoRa, and feeds a laptop app that shows the whole group’s trails and last known positions.
No cell service, subscription, or phone required. 

Problem Statement: 
In remote hiking and camping areas, cell service is often unavailable, so groups that separate cannot see where each 
other are, and nobody holds a record of where the group has been. If someone fails to return, the people who need to find them 
have no last known position, trail, or way to see which areas have already been covered

